WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.438
Preference optimization usually asks one objective to supervise an entire answer.

2
00:00:05.438 --> 00:00:07.680
TFPO starts from a different premise:

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.791
different tokens play different roles, so they should not all receive

4
00:00:11.791 --> 00:00:13.286
the same training signal.

5
00:00:14.083 --> 00:00:19.264
Reasoning tokens determine whether an explanation is helpful and well justified.

6
00:00:19.264 --> 00:00:22.151
Final answers, option letters, schema keys,

7
00:00:22.151 --> 00:00:27.924
and code fragments often need likelihood anchoring to remain stable and parseable.

8
00:00:27.924 --> 00:00:33.401
Applying one sequence-level preference signal everywhere can make these roles interfere.

9
00:00:34.183 --> 00:00:38.127
TFPO adds a lightweight gate to every response token.

10
00:00:38.127 --> 00:00:42.715
Low gate values send more weight to a DPO-style preference objective.

11
00:00:42.715 --> 00:00:45.988
High values emphasize chosen-response likelihood.

12
00:00:45.988 --> 00:00:50.117
In effect, reasoning-sensitive spans receive preference shaping,

13
00:00:50.117 --> 00:00:53.656
while answer-bearing spans receive stronger anchoring.

14
00:00:54.417 --> 00:00:58.516
The route is learned from preference pairs, without token labels.

15
00:00:58.516 --> 00:01:02.588
Targeted ablations show what each regularizer controls.

16
00:01:02.588 --> 00:01:09.160
Removing the ratio penalty raises budget violations from 1.6 to 36.1 percent.

17
00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:12.781
Removing total variation increases local switching.

18
00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:18.980
Removing entropy raises early saturation from 6.4 to 52.1 percent.

19
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:25.299
TFPO reaches the highest 10-benchmark average of 88.00,

20
00:01:25.299 --> 00:01:32.194
versus 83.08 for SimPO and 83.52 for SimPO plus NLL.

21
00:01:32.194 --> 00:01:34.913
Results average 3 training seeds.

22
00:01:34.913 --> 00:01:39.650
BBH, GSM8K, and MATH use fixed 200-prompt subsets with

23
00:01:39.650 --> 00:01:41.756
4 samples per prompt.

24
00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:46.472
Code benchmarks use 20 samples per problem to estimate pass@1.

25
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:51.465
The routing claim is tested independently of benchmark accuracy.

26
00:01:51.465 --> 00:01:58.590
On 1,000 blind annotated responses, the content gate reaches 0.85 AUPRC,

27
00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:03.772
versus 0.55 for the strongest strict position-only control.

28
00:02:03.772 --> 00:02:06.560
Moving the answer to the beginning,

29
00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:10.743
middle, or end changes TFPO's score by only 0.02.

30
00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:16.199
The same routing recipe is trained independently on Qwen,

31
00:02:16.199 --> 00:02:18.265
Llama, and Mistral backbones.

32
00:02:18.265 --> 00:02:23.219
TFPO is strongest in every reported AlpacaEval and Arena-Hard column,

33
00:02:23.219 --> 00:02:28.172
suggesting that the result is not tied to one tokenizer,

34
00:02:28.172 --> 00:02:30.649
instruction-tuning recipe, or model family.

35
00:02:31.417 --> 00:02:38.995
With a Qwen3-VL backbone, TFPO reaches the best multimodal average of 71.03.

36
00:02:38.995 --> 00:02:42.115
The first case illustrates answer formatting,

37
00:02:42.115 --> 00:02:46.276
not visual-counting accuracy: TFPO supplies an option letter.

38
00:02:46.276 --> 00:02:49.369
The map case illustrates visual grounding.

39
00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:54.782
In the numerical case, both TFPO and SimPO reach the correct answer,

40
00:02:54.782 --> 00:02:57.037
but TFPO is more concise.

41
00:02:57.817 --> 00:03:02.031
Across 4 matched samples per prompt,

42
00:03:02.031 --> 00:03:07.650
TFPO reaches 91.97 answer agreement, 86.33 majority accuracy,

43
00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:10.460
and 90.56 average accuracy.

44
00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.699
Explanation diversity reaches 62.33.

45
00:03:14.699 --> 00:03:20.898
Results average over BBH, GSM8K, and MATH, then 3 training seeds.

46
00:03:20.898 --> 00:03:24.983
Missing or invalid generations remain in the denominator.

47
00:03:25.783 --> 00:03:31.224
TFPO reframes preference optimization as token-level credit assignment between preference

48
00:03:31.224 --> 00:03:33.400
shaping and likelihood anchoring.

49
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:36.957
The results show improved performance and answer stability.

50
00:03:36.957 --> 00:03:40.103
Strict position controls, blind gold spans,

51
00:03:40.103 --> 00:03:44.821
and answer-position counterfactuals provide complementary evidence that the learned

52
00:03:44.821 --> 00:03:46.918
route tracks answer-bearing content.
